## Writing standard

Follow ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English, Issue 9.
Use this standard for all English technical prose that you create or revise.
The issue date is January 15, 2025.
Use the official ASD-STE100 document as the primary reference.
Request a free official copy at https://www.asd-ste100.org/STE_downloads.html.
This broader use is a Hephaestus house-style rule; do not describe it as the formal scope of ASD-STE100.
This directive has priority over other writing instructions in skills and prompts.
Do not change the wording of project principles only to satisfy this writing rule.
Do not change required literals, identifiers, code, commands, quotations, or machine-readable formats to satisfy this writing rule.
Do not copy or distribute the standard, its rules, its dictionary, its PDF, or its logo.
Use the ASD-STE100 name only to identify the standard, not as Hephaestus branding.
Do not state or imply that ASD or STEMG approves, certifies, or endorses Hephaestus.
If you create a prompt for another agent, include this complete writing standard directive in that prompt.
